The '''Old Confederal Cabildo''', also known as the '''Confederal House''', is a historic government building, and now a museum, in the [[Hisbanya]] borough of [[Castejón]]. It housed the [[Confederal Congress]] from the mid-19th century until [[Storming of the Baliscan Cabildo|it's destruction]] during the events of the [[Tragic Week]] of the [[Baliscan Revolution]]. It was ultimately replaced by the [[Baliscan Cabildo|current cabildo building]], which was constructed from 1924-1929.

Restored in the 1950s, the Old Cabildo now houses the [[Social Revolution Museum]], dedicated to social and political movements in Balisca dating back to colonization. 

